01:01:51.700 --> 01:01:53.470
- You think she found my lesson?

01:01:53.470 --> 01:01:54.510
- Leave her to me.

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:08.440
What did you mean by that crack you just made to Helen?

01:02:08.440 --> 01:02:10.090
Come out of the whack.

01:02:10.090 --> 01:02:14.480
Did you find him in the hall after the fire drill night before last?

01:02:14.480 --> 01:02:15.460
No, oh no.

01:02:15.460 --> 01:02:16.460
Don't lie to me.

01:02:16.460 --> 01:02:18.280
Then come out with it.

01:02:18.280 --> 01:02:20.170
I found some letters.

01:02:20.170 --> 01:02:23.130
What did you do with them?

01:02:23.130 --> 01:02:25.130
I gave them to Faith Morgan.

01:02:25.130 --> 01:02:27.100
You skunk.

01:02:32.460 --> 01:02:32.980
Hello, Stella.

01:02:34.130 --> 01:02:35.610
Yeah, I talked to you in Eva.

01:02:36.080 --> 01:02:36.540
I know.

01:02:37.410 --> 01:02:39.170
Little Rath has already been here.

01:02:40.170 --> 01:02:42.170
And she's passed with flying colors.

01:02:43.630 --> 01:02:45.090
Oh, yeah, I had to.

01:02:46.200 --> 01:02:50.760
She knows enough to make an impossible scandal with that nasty, sex-starved imagination of hers.

01:02:52.460 --> 01:02:54.760
At least I saved the remnants of my conscience.

01:02:55.800 --> 01:03:00.000
All the other half-wits and the mewling morons of the class got the same dispensaries.

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:12.920
I won't give it to one and not the other. Hereafter, my course will be known as a soft snap, to be joyously elected by all the house guests that visit these halls.

01:03:12.920 --> 01:03:21.430
Oh, Gil, I made a mess of things. Your work is everything to you, it's your whole life.

01:03:21.430 --> 01:03:28.770
We've always had such high ideals and lived up to them, until I came along.

01:03:28.770 --> 01:03:30.000
Do you not?

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:40.670
to blame as much as I my fault more than yours but it's been worth it hasn't it there I'm not sure

01:03:40.670 --> 01:03:53.180
Gil why your your life is here you've always said that college should should come first you see

01:03:53.180 --> 01:04:00.000
I've begun to get your creed too Jerry then come on

01:04:00.250 --> 01:04:04.610
Come in.

01:04:04.610 --> 01:04:08.230
Good afternoon.

01:04:08.230 --> 01:04:10.370
That's much better, thank you.

01:04:10.370 --> 01:04:12.370
How's your poor arm today?

01:04:12.370 --> 01:04:14.370
Was it awfully exciting?

01:04:14.370 --> 01:04:16.370
Yes.

01:04:16.370 --> 01:04:18.370
Oh, I do hope you like the things better this time.

01:04:18.370 --> 01:04:20.370
Yes, I hope so.

01:04:20.370 --> 01:04:22.370
Here's my theme.

01:04:22.370 --> 01:04:26.180
Yes, thank you.

01:04:26.180 --> 01:04:27.620
Stella, Babs is outside looking all over for you.

01:04:35.080 --> 01:04:36.140
- What's up, Babs?

01:04:36.140 --> 01:04:37.380
- Eva's found the letters,

01:04:37.380 --> 01:04:39.520
and she's given them to Faith Morgan.

01:04:39.520 --> 01:04:40.850
- What?

01:04:40.850 --> 01:04:43.200
- I had to pull her ear off to make her confess,

01:04:43.200 --> 01:04:48.220
and I would have if I'd known what to do with it.

01:04:48.220 --> 01:04:50.130
- All right, I'll see, Faith.

01:05:05.560 --> 01:05:06.560
- Hello, Stella.

01:05:06.560 --> 01:05:17.220
- Hello, Faith.

01:05:17.220 --> 01:05:18.740
Tuck gave you some letters.

01:05:18.740 --> 01:05:21.620
- Yes.

01:05:21.620 --> 01:05:24.370
- You aren't gonna turn them over to the board, are you?

01:05:24.370 --> 01:05:26.250
- I have to, Stella.

01:05:26.250 --> 01:05:28.390
They confirm the alumni award.

01:05:28.390 --> 01:05:30.000
You know, it's the highest honor we have.

01:05:30.410 --> 01:05:32.230
And it mustn't go to Helen if she's unworthy.

01:05:33.820 --> 01:05:36.910
Helen? What has she got to do with the letters?

01:05:37.340 --> 01:05:38.920
There's no doubt they were hers.

01:05:40.630 --> 01:05:43.950
Helen, could I see them?

01:05:46.380 --> 01:05:47.240
Please, Faith.

01:05:47.730 --> 01:05:49.110
If they're what I think they are,

01:05:49.330 --> 01:05:52.560
I can save you from doing something that you'll always be sorry for.

01:05:59.210 --> 01:05:59.750
All right.

01:06:23.480 --> 01:06:24.870
- Oh, that's contemptible.

01:06:24.870 --> 01:06:26.370
Why shouldn't I take them?

01:06:26.370 --> 01:06:30.000
They're my letters, yours.

01:06:30.920 --> 01:06:31.720
Why, certainly.

01:06:32.150 --> 01:06:34.630
I never gave you the wild idea there were Helen's.

01:06:35.530 --> 01:06:38.520
What about the reference to the alumni award?

01:06:39.120 --> 01:06:41.480
I suppose that means a lot to you.

01:06:44.000 --> 01:06:46.530
Faith, you don't know what it means to me.

01:06:48.500 --> 01:06:49.240
You know Helen.

01:06:49.790 --> 01:06:51.510
You know what kind of a girl she is.

01:06:51.910 --> 01:06:54.270
She wouldn't do anything that wasn't decent and straight.

01:06:55.060 --> 01:06:55.580
Don't you?

01:06:56.250 --> 01:06:58.440
I'd always thought so.

01:07:00.190 --> 01:07:01.090
I know her.

01:07:01.090 --> 01:07:07.010
I've watched her for over two years, slating at her work, giving up all her fun because

01:07:07.010 --> 01:07:08.010
she had ideals.

01:07:08.010 --> 01:07:15.110
Show me any other girl in this college who cares for scholarships the way she does.

01:07:15.110 --> 01:07:21.850
Oh, I'm silly and frivolous, but I've come to love and admire her more than any other

01:07:21.850 --> 01:07:23.300
girl I've ever seen.

01:07:23.300 --> 01:07:29.800
Why, you want to know as well as I that Helen couldn't do anything that wasn't fine.

01:07:33.390 --> 01:07:35.690
I'll be put at the letters to the disciplinary committee.

01:07:36.500 --> 01:07:37.920
I've got to take them there.

01:07:38.280 --> 01:07:39.760
I can't lie about it.

01:07:40.510 --> 01:07:44.280
You won't have to lie because I'm going over there with you.

01:08:08.480 --> 01:08:10.640
- Good afternoon, Ms. Morgan. - Good afternoon.

01:08:10.640 --> 01:08:26.400
- Good afternoon, Ms. Aynes. - Good afternoon.

01:08:26.400 --> 01:08:29.800
It's, uh, I heard in the letters that were found

01:08:30.890 --> 01:08:41.130
my door. Have you the letters, Miss Morgan? No, she hasn't. I took them from her. They

01:08:41.130 --> 01:08:47.330
are so personal, I can't let anyone read them. But they are extremely important. We

01:08:47.330 --> 01:08:54.640
must know their contents. But I can't let you read them. They are my letters. I am

01:08:54.640 --> 01:09:00.000
willing to admit everything that is in them. I'll even admit I spent the night

01:09:00.480 --> 01:09:02.990
Out on the beach with a man several weeks ago.

01:09:03.750 --> 01:09:08.980
I can't tell you anymore.

01:09:12.000 --> 01:09:15.960
I am leaving college this afternoon.

01:09:24.360 --> 01:09:24.620
Goodbye.

01:10:02.170 --> 01:10:04.230
That's pretty stiff to take.

01:10:04.230 --> 01:10:09.920
Oh, I've got other reasons to leave in college,

01:10:09.920 --> 01:10:13.730
even if the letters haven't been found.

01:10:13.730 --> 01:10:20.450
After all, I haven't been such a credit to Winston.

01:10:20.450 --> 01:10:29.640
I called you a selfish one.

01:10:31.820 --> 01:10:32.400
I'm...

01:11:19.450 --> 01:11:30.000
- Now where are you going college?

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:32.310
I never should have come, never.

01:11:32.720 --> 01:11:34.140
All I've done is to cause trouble.

01:11:36.000 --> 01:11:37.690
Now I've got to kill him for trouble.

01:11:39.130 --> 01:11:40.710
It's time I left before he caused me more.

01:11:41.880 --> 01:11:42.460
Does he know?

01:11:43.440 --> 01:11:46.210
Yes, he knows.

01:12:00.350 --> 01:12:06.370
Yeah, what I was cleaning up things.

01:12:06.370 --> 01:12:11.180
Next time, don't write.

01:12:11.180 --> 01:12:12.230
Telegraph.

01:12:12.230 --> 01:12:13.310
It's safer.

01:12:13.310 --> 01:12:17.840
Let me help you.

01:12:17.840 --> 01:12:25.700
Hurts me.

01:12:35.020 --> 01:12:36.440
Would be a shield cause no trouble.

01:12:38.320 --> 01:12:41.380
We'll be wretched here without you, Stella.

01:12:43.280 --> 01:12:45.910
Oh, we'll see a lot of each other vacation.

01:12:47.740 --> 01:12:49.940
You'll be famous around here when you win the award.

01:12:51.140 --> 01:12:52.260
You've got to do big things.

01:12:56.130 --> 01:12:56.750
You and Gil,

01:14:01.880 --> 01:14:03.960
You know, you're a most inept little liar.

01:14:05.960 --> 01:14:07.960
And you didn't expect me to believe that, did you?

01:14:08.920 --> 01:14:10.550
Aren't you even angry?

01:14:10.710 --> 01:14:11.770
No, I'm glad.

01:14:12.330 --> 01:14:14.810
I'm glad you had the courage to make me come to a decision.

01:14:16.000 --> 01:14:19.190
I'm leaving college, too, at the end of the term.

01:14:19.580 --> 01:14:20.420
But you'll work.

01:14:20.880 --> 01:14:21.320
Work?

01:14:22.250 --> 01:14:23.910
There'll be plenty ahead for both of us.

01:14:24.260 --> 01:14:25.920
But we'll probably do more good.

01:14:27.650 --> 01:14:30.000
We, um, we start next June.

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:31.560
on an expedition to Malaya.

01:14:32.420 --> 01:14:35.690
No morons, but plenty of savages.

01:14:36.790 --> 01:14:38.470
We'll be right at home.

01:14:40.310 --> 01:14:42.330
I see you found her all right, sir.

01:14:43.620 --> 01:14:43.920
Yeah.

01:14:45.410 --> 01:14:46.090
For keeps.

01:14:54.260 --> 01:14:55.800
My savages.

01:15:08.990 --> 01:15:09.510
Minena.
